From 996663ad36c619c347fe152af58c177a8e56d90d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AmazoniaDB improvement session <amazoniadb-session@local>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 01:59:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Add dark mode (site-wide, all 9 pages, all 3 locales)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- New theme.js, shared across en/es/pt-br (one file — only the toggle
  button's aria-label is locale-specific, picked at runtime from
  <html lang>, matched on the primary subtag so it isn't thrown off
  by the existing 'es' vs 'es-419' inconsistency between
  es/candidates.html and its sibling pages).
- Applied before first paint: a small inline script in <head> (right
  after <meta charset>, identical on every page) reads
  localStorage, falls back to prefers-color-scheme, and sets
  data-theme on <html> synchronously — no flash of the wrong theme.
- If the visitor has never explicitly toggled on a device, it keeps
  following the OS-level scheme live (e.g. system switches at
  sunset) instead of freezing whatever it was on first visit; an
  explicit click always wins from then on and is what gets persisted.
- Toggle button (sun/moon, aria-pressed) added to the header on all
  9 HTML pages (index/submit/candidates x en/es/pt-br), next to the
  language switcher.

Dark palette (tokens in styles.css) was chosen and verified
computationally, not eyeballed: every text/background pairing hits
WCAG AA (most land well past it, several near AAA). Border and
shadow tokens were tuned separately since those aren't subject to
text-contrast rules — they follow the same subtle-not-invisible
relationship the existing light mode already uses between --line
and --paper.

Two things are intentionally fixed regardless of theme rather than
inverted with everything else, because they're not really page
content — they're a permanent design decision either way:
- .principles-section (the dark brand panel) — decoupled onto new
  --panel/--on-panel* tokens instead of reusing --forest, since
  --forest itself needs to become a light color in dark mode and
  reusing it here would have put light text on a light panel.
- .record-preview pre (the JSON/code preview) — decoupled onto new
  --code-bg/--code-text, for the same reason it was previously
  hardcoded off --ink. Also gained a 1px border, because in dark
  mode the surrounding card and this block are close enough in
  value (~1.07 contrast ratio) to visually blend without one.

Also fixed several hardcoded colors that would have broken outright
under the new dark palette rather than just looking suboptimal:
card backgrounds (#fff), the primary-button hover state, and the
input placeholder color were all pulled onto tokens.

Verified with a full headless test (theme-test.mjs, removed before
this commit — same reasoning as the earlier feature commit: no
existing test/dependency setup in this project) covering:
OS-preference detection, stored-preference override, click-to-toggle
with aria-pressed and localStorage persistence, and the correct
label across all 9 pages including the es/candidates.html lang-tag
edge case. Also re-ran the full feature-commit smoke test afterward
to confirm nothing regressed.
